  Final report:
    I built the blog and checked it: the front page and both posts return 200 at https://localhost:44317, and every block renders with no "Could not render component" fallback.
    
    **Schema** (built with the `umbraco` MCP server, and each type read back after saving):
    - **Blocks:** three block types, filed in the Blocks folder: Rich Text Block, Image Block (image and caption) and Quote Block (quote and attribution).
    - **Block grid:** one Block Grid data type, "Blog Body Grid", that allows those three blocks.
    - **Page types**, filed in Pages, each with its own template using a shared `layout` template:
      - **Blog Front Page:** title and a block grid body.
      - **Blog Post:** title, publish date, excerpt, listing image and a block grid body.
    - **Where pages can go:** the front page type is allowed under Site Root, and the post type under the front page type.
    
    **Media:** I imported 5 photos from `unsplash/` into a "Blog" media folder.
    
    **Content** (built with `umbraco-editor`, and each page checked with `get-page`):
    - **"The MCP Blog" (`/`):** an intro paragraph and a photo, followed by a list of posts, newest first.
    - **"MCP Is the USB-C of AI" (`/mcp-is-the-usb-c-of-ai/`):** 5 blocks: text, image, text, quote, text.
    - **"Why MCP Makes Your CMS Talk Back" (`/why-mcp-makes-your-cms-talk-back/`):** 5 blocks: text, quote, text, image, text.
    
    Every rich-text block has several paragraphs, and every photo has a caption crediting the photographer. All three pages are published. The front page (not WWW) has the domain `/`.
    
    **Code**, following AGENTS.md:
    - **Adapters:** one per block in `Views/Partials/blockgrid/Components/` (`richTextBlock`, `imageBlock`, `quoteBlock`). Each has the required `@using` and `@inherits UmbracoViewPage<BlockGridItem<…>>` lines and contains no markup.
    - **Components:** one ViewComponent per block in `ViewComponents/`, with the markup in `Views/Shared/Components/<Name>/Default.cshtml`.
    - **View models:** plain classes in `Models/Blocks/`.
    - **Pages:** rendered with `GetBlockGridHtmlAsync`, and all image URLs come from `GetCropUrl()`.
    
    **Checks:**
    - Both `dotnet build` runs had 0 errors and 0 warnings.
    - `npm install` and `npm run build` succeeded, and the compiled CSS contains the classes used in the views.
    - With curl, each page renders all its blocks and shows its own title. The stylesheet and the front page's images (including both post listing images) returned 200. I didn't fetch the in-post image files individually, but their URLs are generated the same way.
    
    **To view it:** Umbraco is running in the background now. Open https://localhost:44317/. The backoffice is at `/umbraco` (admin@example.com / 1234567890).
    
    **Issues:**
    - My first attempt to publish the front page together with its child pages came back "Publish cancelled", most likely a confirmation prompt that wasn't answered. Publishing each page on its own worked.
    - `get-page` returns an empty `publishedUrls` for all three pages. The URLs above work over curl.
    - I didn't check whether uSync exported the new schema, which it's supposed to do automatically.

