  Final report:
    The blog is built and running at https://localhost:44317/. I fetched `/` and both posts with `curl -k`: all returned 200, none contained "Could not render component", and every block rendered. I haven't looked at it in a browser, so the visual styling is unchecked.
    
    **What's on the site**
    - **Front page** (`/`, "The MCP Blog"): a welcome rich-text block and a "Latest posts" grid of two cards, each with a listing image, date, title and excerpt. Cards link to the posts.
    - **Post 1** (`/why-mcp-is-awesome/`): 5 body blocks, namely rich text, an image with caption, rich text, a quote, and rich text.
    - **Post 2** (`/mcp-makes-tools-talk/`): the same 5-block pattern.
    - The front page and both posts show as Published in `get-page` with their values. The domain `/` is on the front page, not WWW.
    - The image URLs on the post page (a listing image and the in-body image) loaded with 200.
    
    **How it's built**
    - **Types** (`umbraco` server):
      - Block element types `richTextBlock`, `imageBlock` and `quoteBlock` sit in the Blocks folder.
      - A "Blog Body Block Grid" data type allows those three blocks.
      - `blogFrontPage` and `blogPost` sit in Pages, each with a `blocks` property and its own template.
      - `siteRoot` allows the front page type, and the front page type allows the post type.
    - **Media** (`umbraco` server): 4 Unsplash photos are in a "Blog Images" folder, credited in the captions.
    - **Content** (`umbraco-editor` server): pages, blocks and publishing.
    - **Razor and C#:**
      - Pages render the block grid with `Html.GetBlockGridHtmlAsync(Model, "blocks")`.
      - Each block has an adapter in `Views/Partials/blockgrid/Components/<alias>.cshtml`, a plain model in `Models/Blocks/`, a ViewComponent in `ViewComponents/`, and its markup in `Views/Shared/Components/<Name>/Default.cshtml`.
      - There is also a shared `_Layout.cshtml`.
    - **Builds:** `npm run build` ran after the views were written, and `dotnet build` passes with 0 errors.
    
    **Things to know**
    - Umbraco is running as a background task in this session, and it stops when the session ends.
    - My first `dotnet build` after writing the views failed on `Model.Parent` in `blogPost.cshtml`, because `Parent` is a method in this Umbraco version. I switched it to `AncestorOrSelf<BlogFrontPage>()`.
    - The block grid's block config (column spans and so on) is minimal. I wrote it without a reference data type to copy, and it saved and read back fine. I haven't opened it in the backoffice.
    - I didn't check that the Blog Body Block Grid data type landed under `/Custom/…`. The read-back doesn't show a parent, and I relied on the project's save handler.
    - I didn't check that the uSync export files were written.
    
    Nothing failed repeatedly, and I made no changes outside the MCP servers and the project folder.

